---
source: crates/jailint/tests/rules.rs
---
error[element_count_as_bytes]: `values.count` counts `s32` elements, but this argument is a number of bytes
  --> tests/lint/element_count_as_bytes/bad.jai:8:36
   |
 8 |     memcpy(dest.data, values.data, values.count);
   |                                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: multiply by the element size: `values.count * size_of(s32)`
   |
 7   copy_values :: (dest: [] s32, values: [] s32) {
 8 ~     memcpy(dest.data, values.data, values.count * size_of(s32));
 9   }
   |
   = note: `element_count_as_bytes` is `deny` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/element_count_as_bytes

error[element_count_as_bytes]: `weights.count` counts `float32` elements, but this argument is a number of bytes
  --> tests/lint/element_count_as_bytes/bad.jai:12:29
   |
12 |     memset(weights.data, 0, weights.count);
   |                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: multiply by the element size: `weights.count * size_of(float32)`
   |
11   clear :: (weights: [] float) {
12 ~     memset(weights.data, 0, weights.count * size_of(float32));
13   }
   |
   = note: `element_count_as_bytes` is `deny` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/element_count_as_bytes

error[element_count_as_bytes]: `a.count` counts `Pair` elements, but this argument is a number of bytes
  --> tests/lint/element_count_as_bytes/bad.jai:16:35
   |
16 |     return memcmp(a.data, b.data, a.count) == 0;
   |                                   ^^^^^^^
   |
help: multiply by the element size: `a.count * size_of(Pair)`
   |
15   same :: (a: [4] Pair, b: [4] Pair) -> bool {
16 ~     return memcmp(a.data, b.data, a.count * size_of(Pair)) == 0;
17   }
   |
   = note: `element_count_as_bytes` is `deny` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/element_count_as_bytes
